e progression.'],engineFeedback:['Dependency-free native rendering, headless fixed stepping, and the TV Shell provided a useful integrated foundation.','The overhead view is the x/y flight plane even for a side-on spacecraft game; native private pause behavior needed careful integration.','The deterministic mission director and authenticated shared-ship authority with complete snapshots.','Keeping Shell input suppression, local pause, touch and live shared-world lifecycle consistent.','No vendor engine changes; game-owned adapters extend collision, content, input, presentation and audio.','A documented shared-ship role/input adapter would simplify simultaneous cooperative games.'],promptFeedback:['The concrete rescue fantasy and explicit full-journey acceptance checks.','The source title also refers to unrelated games; the supplied platform and references resolve it.','Completing and verifying all input families and shared-world lifecycle in one self-contained artifact.','Keep the detailed acceptance criteria, and provide a machine-readable requirement checklist alongside them.'],aiHub:{name:'Freedom Warp Rescue',tagline:'Two drives. One ship. Bring them home.',description:'Thread a rescue craft through living minefields, free fragile crystal captives, and break the prison carrier. Fly solo or share steering, cannon and hyperspace with a co-pilot.',type:'Game',genre:'Shooter',source:'Freedom Fighters\"'! (1982)'\"',series:'',players:'1–2',controls:'WASD / left stick steer; mouse / right stick aim; click, Space or R2 / square fire; Shift / L2 hyperspace; Escape / Options pause.',tags:['2d','arcade','sci-fi','co-op','side-scrolling','boss fights']}};\nfs.writeFileSync('exit-interview.json',JSON.stringify(data,null,2)+'\\\\n');\nJS\nnode 'Freedom-Warp-Rescue-Freedom-Fighters-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-023037/tools/build.mjs' --verbose\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
