{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_82","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"node --input-type=module - <<'JS'\nimport fs from 'node:fs';\nconst p='exit-interview.json',r=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(p,'utf8'));\nr.testingFeedback=[\n'16 unique issues fixed across functional, protocol and visual checks and implementation review; the issue ledger records each defect once.',\n'1 critical/game-breaking issue: closing the pause overlay could leave the world invisibly paused. It is fixed and covered by a real controller resume test.',\n'The action-driven full operation in the exported HTML and two actual Hub browser copies: it proved rescues, replacement recovery, every carrier phase, shared score and a single ending without invulnerability or objective shortcuts.',\n'Syntax-only checks were least informative about actual play; they could not detect viewport clipping, invisible pause state or network role handoff errors.'\n];\nr.engineFeedback=[\n'The dependency-free pixel renderer, native fixed-step headless execution, shaded assets, synth buses and TV Shell form a useful integrated foundation.',\n'The overhead view is the correct x/y plane for this side-on flight game. I initially combined Shell scaling with viewport-height limits incorrectly and needed to reconcile custom pause state with native overlay close behavior.',\n'The deterministic mission director, swept rescue/combat resolution and authenticated shared-ship authority with complete snapshots.',\n'Keeping native Shell input suppression, shared-world live simulation, touch projection and local pause lifecycle consistent across all devices.',\n'No vendor engine code changed. Game-owned adapters extend collision, authored content, native actor/part animation, input roles, audio and Hub transport.',\n'A documented shared-ship role/input adapter plus scaled scrolling-menu example would simplify simultaneous cooperative games.'\n];\nr.promptFeedback=[\n'The clear rescue fantasy, restrained mechanics and concrete full-journey acceptance checks made implementation and verification decisions specific.',\n'The source title also names unrelated games; the specified Odyssey²/Videopac platform and archival references resolved that ambiguity. Exact original sound remained unknown because recording playback was inaccessible.',\n'Integrating and verifying every input family, checkpoint lifetime and authoritative multiplayer journey inside one self-contained artifact.',\n'Keep the acceptance detail and add a machine-readable requirement checklist with the supplied engine and Hub revision manifests.'\n];\nfs.writeFileSync(p,JSON.stringify(r,null,2)+'\\\\n');\nJS\ncd 'Freedom-Warp-Rescue-Freedom-Fighters-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-023037' && biome format --write src tests/*.mjs tools/*.mjs package.json identity.json biome.json && biome check src tests/*.mjs tools/*.mjs package.json identity.json biome.json && ruff check tests/browser.py && node tools/verify.mjs\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
