{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_106","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nPath('PROGRESS.md').write_text('''# Freedom Warp Rescue — complete\n\nTitle selected by a cryptographic random draw from exactly 50 candidates. No candidate list was published.\n\nDevelopment directory and final basename:\n\"'`Freedom-Warp-Rescue-Freedom-Fighters-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-023037`\n\n## Hand-in\n\n- Root HTML with the exact basename above: self-contained, no runtime downloads, opens directly from file://.\n- Root exit-interview.json: final canonical source information, all ordered feedback answers and catalogue metadata; embedded identically in About/Credits.\n- All implementation, vendor code, tools, tests, logs and screenshots are in the development directory.\n\n## Final verification\n\n**106/106 checks passed** on the final artifact. Command from the development directory:\n\n`node tools/verify.mjs` (also `npm test`).\n\nThe quiet runner rebuilds, runs changed suites only using source fingerprints, and prints failures plus one count. artifacts/verification.json contains individual results; artifacts/delivery-manifest.json records the exact final HTML byte length/hash and revisions.\n\nVerified journeys:\n\n- Full native and exported-browser ordinary-action operation with all 13 rescues: 12 required and the optional high-risk signal. Every enemy, mine pattern and carrier phase appears; extraction and real ending reached without invulnerability or objective injection.\n- Full 180-second Evasion with cannon unavailable, rescues, hyperspace and terminal result.\n- Native collision/rescue priority, exactly-once score, fragile crystals, committed swept hyperspace, release latches, grace, owner-only collapse, per-layer mine score cap, replacements, terminal races and deterministic checkpoint reconstruction.\n- Native and browser pad/keyboard/mouse controls, real rebinding/prompts, two-pad and keyboard+pad couch roles, swap/disconnect/sole takeover.\n- Phone/tablet multitouch first rescue, real warp, cancellation, contextual control and Menu. Final phone HUD no longer overlaps Menu.\n- Native TV Shell title/pause/settings/controls/credits/dev/results/failure; real pointer dev single-step, live slider and reset. Long scaled panels scroll correctly.\n- Exact 10-second isolated looping attract; consumed exits for keyboard, pointer, pad and touch; no saves or best-score contamination.\n- Procedural music/effects/gibberish OfflineAudioContext render: finite, non-silent, bounded. Native music starts at 0.10; pause/end clear sources.\n- Five actual supplied Hub harness scenarios: two players, 150±50ms/5% loss, host leave, no-local-player server authority, solo.\n- Two actual Hub browser copies completed the operation through their own semantic seat intentions and real transport. Authoritative ledgers, outcome and score agree; finish exactly once; message-size/rate limits respected; no Hub warnings or page/engine errors.\n- Final package equality, unmodified session client first-script placement/bytes, exact metadata schema/enums and canonical embedded report.\n\nNative presentation 32 checks, frontend 13, network 16, simulation 22; browser frontend 8, final artifact 6, Hub 6, package 3 = 106.\n\nVisual evidence: artifacts/final-visual-*.png, final-phone-hud.png, developer-tools.png and results.png. Reviewed 1920×1080 and phone portrait/landscape; no FPS acceptance gate.\n\n## Documentation and reporting\n\n- docs/research.md records personally read manual/review and inspected original screenshots. The specified recording'\"'s identity was confirmed from metadata, but playback and exact original sound are unknown.\n- Full engine 0.89.1 at 8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691; Hub session 1.4.0/protocol 1 at 35a1047f2067b2af3de3943f0fe452f39105d869. Vendor code unmodified.\n- docs/contracts.md: authority, collision order, state/lifetime, checkpoints and score caps.\n- docs/req